ChannelTerm Electron is licensed under the repository's Apache License 2.0.

The independent npm dependency graph is pinned in package-lock.json. The current
installed JavaScript dependency notices include MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, and Apache-2.0
licenses. Electron uses MIT and includes Chromium and other third-party code
with their own notices.

Menu localization uses Lingui Core 5.9.0 (MIT). Its installed dependency licenses
are included by the same notice collection; no translation service is contacted.
The matching Lingui CLI/config/PO tools are build dependencies, not application
services. npm may also install optional build-tool peers; their installed notices
are retained conservatively. Absent optional packages for other platforms are skipped;
missing required packages or license texts in installed packages remain build errors.

Terminal input encoding uses iconv-lite 0.7.3 (MIT), a pure JavaScript dependency
loaded only in Main. Its license is included in the generated notices below.

Terminal search uses @xterm/addon-search 0.16.0 (MIT), pinned alongside xterm 6.0.0
from the same upstream release commit. It adds no runtime dependencies or native
code. Its installed MIT license is included in the generated notices below.

npm run build collects the installed runtime dependency license texts, including
the Electron npm package license, into dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and copies the
ChannelTerm license into dist/LICENSE. Redistribution of the bundled JavaScript
must retain those files. The generated notices cover the installed production
dependency graph, including packages that the client bundle may not use.

Local desktop packages retain Electron's distributed license (LICENSE.electron.txt
on Windows) and LICENSES.chromium.html and accompanying runtime notices. The
repository THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES is included as resources/HOST_THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
for both Go companions; resources/LICENSE.channelterm carries the Apache-2.0 text.
The bundled JS notices and license remain inside app.asar under dist/.

electron-builder 26.18.0 (MIT) is a pinned build dependency for local unsigned
archives/installers. Its JavaScript dependency graph is not bundled into the app.
The generated NSIS installer uses the unmodified NSIS runtime and plugins under
their upstream licenses, including zlib/libpng and the compression-module terms
with the LZMA linking exception. License terms: https://nsis.sourceforge.io/License
Corresponding tool/source distribution: https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder-binaries/releases/tag/nsis-3.0.4.1
Building packages does not enable signing, publishing or an update service.
